Also possible root cause: OPPO's FUSE manager requires the app to hold "android.permission.MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE" AND the appop; appop is allow... but maybe the appop name for this ROM differs, or Environment.isExternalStorageManager() checks a different state. Let me add debug display: In FilesScreen empty/loading area show error from exception; also PermScreen? Actually quicker on-screen probe: change HomeScreen? No—just FilesScreen error display.

Even quicker: use `adb shell am start -n ...` nothing. Let me just patch load() to capture errors:

```java
act.bg(() -> {
    String err = null;
    ArrayList<File> out = new ArrayList<>();
    try {
        for (File f : Fs.list(d, false)) out.add(f);
