App restarted at 14:03:03, MainActivity displayed. My tap at (153,178) after 3s sleep should have hit 文件 tile. But screenshot still identical to the FilesScreen "读取中" from before...

OH WAIT. I bet the tap DID open FilesScreen, and it's stuck on 读取中 because... hmm no, we fixed permission. Unless the reading actually HANGS: Fs.list(root) → listFiles() blocks. With uid appop "ignore" before, MediaProvider's FUSE might block the app's file operations indefinitely (each listFiles syscall blocks on FUSE deadlock). But new process after appop change...

Actually hold on — maybe the tap did NOT open files: maybe (153,178) hits 文件 tile → FilesScreen shows 读取中… → and reading genuinely hangs forever even with permission (OPPO FUSE quirk where MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE apps need the toggle in Settings UI which writes some additional state).

The identical-file thing makes me suspect the screenshot pipeline. Let me verify by taking two screenshots at different times and comparing hashes — they were identical. And the clock isn't drawn in our app, so static frame is plausible.

Decisive test: `adb shell input swipe` to scroll the file list; if UI responds, screenshot changes. If nothing changes, taps aren't reaching the app at all (then why did the first tap open FilesScreen earlier? Because it did change then — we saw FilesScreen).

So taps work. The screen is FilesScreen stuck at 读取中. The bg thread must be blocked in listFiles. Interesting: FUSE blocking forever happens when the app's FUSE lookups are denied-but-blocked? Unusual but OPPO...

Let me test direct file access timing from adb as a different app that works (MT管理器 bin.mt.plus works on this watch obviously). Hmm.

Actually — WAIT. Critical possibility: my bg executor `Executors.newFixedThreadPool(3)` — load() called... if Fs.list(root) actually THROWS the callback posts error... but the error path requires `d.equals(dir)` — same. Fine.

Let me test whether the FUSE hang theory holds: add a timeout? Can't easily interrupt listFiles. Alternative: check `adb shell ps -A | grep fused`? Better: strace not available.

Practical approach: try legacy storage path. Add to application: `android:requestLegacyExternalStorage="true"` (no effect on 30 w/ FUSE). 

OR use MediaStore-based listing as fallback. For v1 diagnosis, let me add a quick probe screen: FilesScreen shows "权限检查: isExtMgr=..., canRead=..." and does listFiles with a watchdog: run in thread with get() timeout 5s, show "目录访问卡住" if timeout. That tells us definitively.

Actually simpler immediate test without rebuilding: use `am` to broadcast? No.

Hmm, another idea: maybe listFiles isn't hanging; maybe my `act.bg(...)` executor threads are all dead! RejectedExecutionException after force-stop? New process, new pool. If a runnable throws before act.ui, loading stays true. In FilesScreen.load new code catches Throwable around Fs.list. But `sc.reset()` etc fine. So callback MUST run unless Fs.list blocks.

To decide quickly, rebuild with watchdog UI:

```java
act.bg(() -> {
    final ArrayList<File> out = new ArrayList<>();
    final String[] err = new String[1];
    Thread t = new Thread(() -> {
        try { for (File f : Fs.list(d,false)) out.add(f); }
        catch (Throwable ex) { err[0] = String.valueOf(ex); }
    });
    t.start();
    try { t.join(6000); } catch (InterruptedException ignored) {}
    if (t.isAlive()) err[0] = "目录访问超时（FUSE 卡死）";
    ...
});
```

That will tell us. Also display Perm state in header when empty. Rebuild and test.

