```java
private float zoom=1f, panX, panY;
private void applyTransform() {
   float bw = surface.getWidth(), bh = surface.getHeight();
   if (bw<=0) return;
   float maxX = Math.max(0, (bw*zoom - bw)/2f);
   float maxY = Math.max(0, (bh*zoom - bh)/2f);
   panX = clamp(panX, -maxX, maxX); panY = clamp(panY, -maxY, maxY);
   surface.setScaleX(zoom); surface.setScaleY(zoom);
   surface.setTranslationX(panX); surface.setTranslationY(panY);
}
```
Note: translation applies after scale around center; with translation in px of parent. Since surface fills screen (up to 466), maxX = (466*zoom-466)/2 correct.

