private void apply(ArrayList<MediaScan.Item> v) {
    if (v.size() == items.size() && !items.isEmpty()) { loading = false; invalidate(); return; }
    items.clear(); items.addAll(v); loading = false;
    sc.max = ...; sc.clamp(); invalidate();
}
```
Hmm if list content changes but same size... rare, ignore.

Careful: applying twice will reset scroll. Only reset if size changed. Let's implement:

```java
private void apply(ArrayList<MediaScan.Item> v) {
    boolean same = v.size() == items.size();
    if (!same) {
        items.clear();
        items.addAll(v);
        sc.reset();
        sc.max = Math.max(0, items.size() * (ROW_H + GAP) - (BOT - TOP));
        sc.clamp();
    }
    loading = false;
    invalidate();
}
```

Gallery similar with rows.

