rawContent.text:
Bug: prev/next just restart current song. Look at MusicService: NEXT: `if (index < paths.size()-1) playCurrent();` — playCurrent uses `index` — that's fine, plays next. But symptom: replays same song. Why? paths list: when user tapped a row, MusicScreen sets MusicService.paths = full list and start(idx). prev/next call playCurrent with updated index? NEXT doesn't increment index! `if (index < paths.size()-1) playCurrent();` — playCurrent() plays paths.get(index) — index unchanged! Bug: should be index++ then playCurrent. PREV similarly index--.

Fix:
```java
} else if ("NEXT".equals(act)) {
    if (index < paths.size() - 1) { index++; playCurrent(); }
} else if ("PREV".equals(act)) {
    if (index > 0) { index--; playCurrent(); }
}
```
Also onCompletion auto-advance: `if (index < paths.size()-1) playCurrent();` — also doesn't increment! Same bug. Fix: index++ then playCurrent. Also loop at end: maybe wrap to 0? Keep stop at last? Better wrap: index = (index+1) % paths.size(). And prev at 0 wraps to last? Keep simple: next wraps, prev wraps.

Build v1.12, install, verify.

